---
source: tests/help_pages.rs
description: "a command's -h and --help pages as this build renders them at 100 columns without color; any change to an about, a flag, a value, a heading or the layout changes them: review with cargo insta review, or re-accept with INSTA_UPDATE=always cargo test --test integration help_pages:: and review git diff tests/snapshots/"
---
==> omaddons completions -h <==
Print a shell completion script

Usage: omaddons completions [OPTIONS] <SHELL>

Arguments:
  <SHELL>  The shell the script is for [possible values: bash, zsh, fish, elvish, powershell]

Examples:
  omaddons completions bash > ~/.local/share/bash-completion/completions/omaddons
  omaddons completions zsh > ~/.zfunc/_omaddons

Global: -t <TARGET>  --json  --dry-run  -v  --quiet  --no-color  --offline  (--help lists them all)
==> omaddons completions --help <==
Print a shell completion script

For bash, zsh, fish, elvish or powershell.

Usage: omaddons completions [OPTIONS] <SHELL>

Arguments:
  <SHELL>
          The shell the script is for
          
          [possible values: bash, zsh, fish, elvish, powershell]

Examples:
  omaddons completions bash >
  "${XDG_DATA_HOME:-$HOME/.local/share}/bash-completion/completions/omaddons"
  omaddons completions zsh > "${fpath[1]}/_omaddons"
  omaddons completions fish > "${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/fish/completions/omaddons.fish"
  omaddons completions bash --json    the script as data: {shell, script}

Commands, subcommands, flags and fixed values complete in every shell. In bash, zsh and
fish, client ids, addon names and plan, backup, transaction and doctor ids complete too,
read from omaddons' own files at each Tab (a client once it is registered). Generate the
script again after upgrading omaddons.

See also: install-completions, help

Global options:
      --json             One JSON envelope on stdout
      --format <FORMAT>  Output format [possible values: json, human]
  -t, --target <TARGET>  The client to act on: id, game mode, family, path, or all [alias: --flavor]
      --dry-run          Show the plan without changing anything
      --actor <ACTOR>    Who is acting: human, agent or widget [env: OMADDONS_ACTOR]
      --reason <TEXT>    Why, recorded verbatim in history
      --offline          Fail any network access [env: OMADDONS_OFFLINE=1]
      --while-running    Allow folder changes while the client runs (never SavedVariables)
      --no-color         No ANSI color
      --no-progress      No progress output
      --progress <MODE>  Progress events on stderr [possible values: json, human, none]
      --quiet            Only errors on stderr
  -v, --verbose...       More detail (repeatable)
  -h, --help             Show help

Learn more: omaddons robot-docs guide
